{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmDV2dhwKnknoWiDZnJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a build plan for a UI component library and business screens. I have a design token set: page bg #F6F5FA, surface #FFFFFF, ink #1A1A1F, secondary #6E6A7C, tertiary #9E99AC, hairline #ECEAF2, track #EFEDF6, brand #6347EB, brand tint #EFEBFE, brand deep #4A32C4, transport #2D8CFF with tint #E8F3FF, bill #F2A03C with tint #FFF2E1, good #1FA97B with tint #E6F6F0, warn #E8833A, over #E5484D.\n\nThe frame is 375 wide, 812 tall. The vertical stack is 44 status bar + 56 header + content region + tab bar 62 + 34 home indicator, so the content region is 812 - 44 - 56 - 62 - 34 = 616, starting at y=100. The tab bar splits into 4 items of 375/4 = 93.75 each.\n\nThe icon and logo clones need a visual check, and a screenshot of the components section confirms clone rendering. That check needs nothing else, and the component build rests only on icon sizes I already know: 24x24 and 48x48. So the screenshot and the component build run together.\n\nFirst batch of components: App/Header 375x56 (back icon at x16, centered title 18 Semibold, add icon at x335, title overridden per instance); App/TabBar 375x62 with a top hairline, each item an icon 24 in tertiary plus a 10px label, active state a 40x28 tint pill behind the icon with brand-colored icon and label, built as variants State=Current and State=Default; App/Segmented 343x44 on #F1EFF7 radius 12 with an active white pill, shadow and brand text, variants for Bills, Payments, Subscription; App/Progress 311x6 with track radius 3 and a child \"Fill\" rect whose width I override per instance; App/PeriodPicker 343x40 with \"September 2020\" 13 Medium plus a 16 chevron on the left and \"Spent $1,812\" on the right; App/MoreRow 343x52 with a 20 icon in a tint circle, \"More categories\" 14 Medium and a chevron; Category/ItemRow 311 wide in vertical auto-layout: a top row with the name 14 Medium and the amount 14 Semibold right-aligned, a 4px progress bar with marginTop 8, and a \"Left $186\" caption 11 tertiary with marginTop 4; RatingChip 22 high, radius 11, padding 8, 11 Semibold text with a dot, variants Good and Not bad.\n\nSecond batch: Category/Card 343 wide, padding 16, a 28 icon tile, name 15 Semibold, total 15 Semibold, and ItemRow instances inside; Bill/SubscriptionRow 343x64 with a 44 white tile holding a 32 logo, name 15 Medium, price 13 secondary, chevron, divider; Bill/Summary 343x96 in brand tint with \"Your monthly payment for subscriptions\" and $58.97 at 28 Bold; Credit/FactorRow 343x64 with name 14 Medium, value 14 Semibold, a rating chip and a detail caption; Credit/Teaser 343x72 with a tile, \"Credit score\", a \"660 · Good\" chip and a chevron.\n\nThe Gauge is 343x200 with a 240x130 arc region. The track is a semicircle path \"M20 120 A100 100 0 0 1 220 120\" stroked 12, round cap, on #EFEDF6. For 660, p = (660 - 400)/450 = 0.5778, giving 104 degrees past 180, so the end point is (120 + 100*cos 284, 120 + 100*sin 284) = (144.2, 23). The value arc runs from (20,120) to (144.2,23) in brand, with a brand dot at the end, 660 at 28 Bold centered, and 400 and 850 labels under the ends.\n\nFor 01_Expenses the content runs about 700 tall: a 44 period row, a budget hero card x16 w343 h150 (\"Monthly budget\", $2,550, \"Left to spend\" $738 at 34px, a progress bar, footer rows), an Auto & transport card ($600; Auto & transport $350 left $186; Auto insurance $250 left $120), a Bill & Utilities card ($320; Sub","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":8554,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":26268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8554}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8c