{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmhi1GnpQgBWdZqpiDb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why the row progress bars all read 180 and why the gauge score sits at y=228. The budget hero fill of 96 is correct (303*0.318=96), so the fault is the nested 'Fill' inside the 'Progress' instance: the setFill resize does not take on that descendant, and 180 is the master default width. I fix it by replacing the 'Progress' instance with inline Track (w311, h4) and Fill (w180, h4) rectangles, then applying widths directly. The gauge score at 228 comes from arcBox being VERTICAL auto layout that stacked children (track 140, then val, dot, score), pushing score past foot at 140. Setting arcBox.layoutMode='NONE' and repositioning score at y=48, rating at 100, foot at 150, height 206 restores it. Screen 01 scrollHeight 890 with contentHeight 616 is fine, and tabChildY [0] is fine.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":3122,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":73484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3122}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8cdba9a76","uuid":"6743176a-f74a-4f52-8f55-c0f55d57b43e","timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:40:13.108Z","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":19373}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmhi1GnpQgBWdZqpiDb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Audit found two real defects: the gauge's inner frame is auto-layout vertical, which stacked the score 228px down, and item-row progress widths stayed at the 180px master value because the fill sits inside a nested instance. Fixing both."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":3122,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":73484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3122}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8cdba9a76","uuid":"4639b741-39a4-4a65-b2ee-a52275d9f0ed","timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:40:14.706Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmhi1GnpQgBWdZqpiDb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DvVWEphrOnOXaMlKGbU0RC","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('4:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst sec = page.findOne(n=>n.name==='Components · Budget');\nfunction hx(h){h=h.replace('#','');return {r:parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255,g:parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255,b:parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255};}\nconst S=(h,a=1)=>({type:'SOLID',color:hx(h),opacity:a});\nconst C={ink:'#1A1A1F',sub:'#6E6A7C',ter:'#9E99AC',brand:'#6347EB',track:'#EEEBF7',white:'#FFFFFF',good:'#1FA97B'};\n\n// ---- 1. Gauge: flatten the arc frame to absolute positioning\nconst gauge=sec.findOne(n=>n.name==='Credit/Gauge');\nconst arcBox=gauge.findOne(n=>n.name==='Arc');\narcBox.layoutMode='NONE';\n[['Track',0],['Value',0],['Knob',0],['Score',44],['Rating',96],['400',118],['850',118]].forEach(()=>{});\nconst sc=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.name==='Score'); sc.y=48; sc.x=0;\nconst rt=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.name==='Rating'); rt.y=100; rt.x=0;\nconst mn=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.characters==='400'); if(mn){mn.x=22;mn.y=118;}\nconst mx=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT'&&n.characters==='850'); if(mx){mx.x=296;mx.y=118;}\nconst tr=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='VECTOR'&&n.name==='Track'); if(tr){tr.x=0;tr.y=0;}\nconst vl=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='VECTOR'&&n.name==='Value'); if(vl){vl.x=0;vl.y=0;}\nconst kn=gauge.findOne(n=>n.type==='ELLIPSE'&&n.name==='Knob'); if(kn){kn.x=Math.round(171.5+104*Math.cos((180-180*0.5777778)*Math.PI/180)-10); kn.y=Math.round(118-104*Math.sin((180-180*0.5777778)*Math.PI/180)-10);}\nconst ft=gauge.findOne(n=>n.name==='Foot'); ft.x=0; ft.y=150;\n\n// ---- 2. Item Row: inline progress rectangles instead of nested instance\nconst ir=sec.findOne(n=>n.name==='Category/Item Row'&&n.type==='COMPONENT');\nconst oldP=ir.findOne(n=>n.name==='Progress'); if(oldP) oldP.remove();\nconst iTrack=figma.createRectangle(); iTrack.name='Track'; iTrack.resize(311,4); iTrack.cornerRadius=2; iTrack.fills=[S(C.track)];\nconst iFill=figma.createRectangle(); iFill.name='Fill'; iFill.resize(180,4); iFill.cornerRadius=2; iFill.fills=[S(C.brand)];\nconst progWrap=figma.createFrame(); progWrap.name='Progress'; progWrap.resize(311,4); progWrap.fills=[]; progWrap.clipsContent=false;\nprogWrap.appendChild(iTrack); progWrap.appendChild(iFill);\nir.appendChild(progWrap);\n// place progress between Top and Left inside vertical stack\nconst kids=ir.children; ir.insertChild(1,progWrap);\n\n// ---- 3. Re-apply fill widths on 01 rows\nconst s1=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('9:85');\nfunction setRowW(row,frac){\n  const p=row.findOne(n=>n.name==='Progress'&&n.type==='FRAME');\n  if(!p) return false;\n  const f=p.findOne(n=>n.name==='Fill'&&n.type==='RECTANGLE');\n  const t=p.findOne(n=>n.name==='Track'&&n.type==='RECTANGLE');\n  if(f) f.resize(Math.max(3,Math.round(311*Math.min(frac,1))),4);\n  return !!f;\n}\nconst rows=[\n ['Auto Card','Row1',350/600],['Auto Card','Row2',250/600],\n ['Bill Card','Row1',1],['Bill Card','Row2',138/160],['Bill Card','Row3',130/160]\n];\nconst res={};\nfor(const [card,rowName,frac] of rows){\n  const cardInst=s1.findOne(n=>n.name===card);\n  const row=cardInst.findOne(n=>n.name===rowName);\n  res[card+'/'+rowName]=setRowW(row,frac);\n}\nreturn JSON.stringify({res, gaugeH:gauge.height, scoreY:sc.y, footY:ft.y, rowKids:ir.children.map(c=>c.name+'@'+Math.round(c.y)+'h'+Math.round(c.height))});","description":"Flatten gauge positioning and replace nested progress instance with inline rectangles","fileKey":"kief32CrRQEGf1OkI4f3T9"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":3122,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":73484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3122}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8cdba9a76","uuid":"69d560e4-4920-4b5e-a45c-62d2d6122ece","timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:40:25.014Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DvVWEphrOnOXaMlKGbU0RC","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
