{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmoKytzCGpOv3Iz4IbM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why every row's progress fill still reads 180 after setRowW reported res: true. The fill sits inside the Progress frame, a child of the row instance, and that frame has no auto-layout, so a resize should stick. The progress wrapper is 311 wide with the fill at 180; the intended width is 233. Matching by name should be safe because p is located as \"Progress\" inside the row, not the hero card's \"Fill\" inside \"Track\". The likely cause is a re-sync of the instance after the master changed. The fix: resize each row's fill and read the width back in the same script; if it still reports 180, delete the rectangle and draw a fresh one with a distinct name. Content scroll height 890 against 616 is fine, and the tab bar at 62 is fine.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":2883,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":82770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2883}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8cdba9a76","uuid":"3a5c8e38-3d8d-489b-93fb-6d563208de36","timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:41:29.001Z","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":14615}
