{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmx8MPWfGGkv6d3pEID","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about resizing the progress Fill rect inside a nested instance. The Fill sits inside the App/Progress component, which sits inside the item-row instance, which sits inside the Category/Card instance. My hypothesis is a constraint conflict: the Fill has constraints STRETCH or layoutSizing FILL/SCALE, so resize returns 180, the master value, instead of the requested width. A plain resize on the master's Fill works; the override on a child of an instance is what fails. I test several strategies on one row: set layoutSizingHorizontal to fixed, set constraints to LEFT, then call resize and resizeWithoutConstraints, and also try resizing the Progress wrapper itself. The diagnostic reports each resulting width so I can see which strategy actually sticks before applying it broadly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":3052,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":88795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3052}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8cdba9a76","uuid":"2b3b736e-6e30-42e9-a906-1bae409c7cc3","timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:43:17.748Z","thinking_duration_ms":15568}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOmx8MPWfGGkv6d3pEID","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01OHzaZdJFVgjmvf0cGiAQLI","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('4:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nconst s1=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('9:85');\nconst row=s1.findOne(n=>n.name==='Auto Card').findOne(n=>n.name==='Row1');\nconst p=row.findOne(n=>n.name==='Progress');\nconst f=p.findOne(n=>n.name==='Fill');\nconst res={};\nres.parent={type:p.type, w:p.width, lm:p.layoutMode, clip:p.clipsContent, sizing:JSON.stringify({h:p.layoutSizingHorizontal,v:p.layoutSizingVertical})};\nres.fill={type:f.type,w:f.width, constraints:JSON.stringify(f.constraints), grow:f.layoutGrow, sizing:JSON.stringify({h:f.layoutSizingHorizontal,v:f.layoutSizingVertical})};\nconst tryIt=(label,fn)=>{ try{ fn(); res[label]={w:f.width, parentW:p.width}; }catch(e){ res[label]='ERR '+e.message; } };\ntryIt('a_plainResize',()=>f.resize(240,4));\ntryIt('b_resizeWOC',()=>f.resizeWithoutConstraints(240,4));\ntryIt('c_setSizingThenResize',()=>{ f.layoutSizingHorizontal='FIXED'; f.resize(240,4); });\ntryIt('d_scale',()=>{ f.rescale(1.3); });\ntryIt('e_parentResize',()=>p.resize(240,4));\ntryIt('f_detachParent',()=>{ const inst=row; res.isInstance=inst.type; });\nreturn JSON.stringify(res,null,1);","description":"Diagnose which resize strategy works on an instance-nested fill rectangle","fileKey":"kief32CrRQEGf1OkI4f3T9"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":3052,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":88795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3052}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2d739e-c576-415e-8b81-afa8cdba9a76","uuid":"1940e476-2ad1-4abb-a29a-cc955468844d"